## KenKen (color groups): generated by rosiegen (WorldSpec, path A: Lean) from the instructor statements.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##  5. You can write a number that is between one and four onto an empty location.
##  6. If the value of a location is absent then the location is empty.
##  11. If the row of a location is the row of a location and the value of the former location is the value of the latter location then you lose.
##  14. If the column of a location is the column of a location and the value of the former location is the value of the latter location then you lose.
##  18. The goal is that all locations are filled.
##  19. If the value of a location is more than zero then the location is filled.
##  23. If the locations in a group are filled and the sum of the values of the group is not ten then you lose.
##  24. If the blocks have the same color then they are in a group.
##
## Assumption ledger:
##   A-L1: "a location ... a location ... the former ... the latter" are two different locations.
##   A-K1: group: the locations with the same color; each must sum to ten when filled.
##   A-K2: The action write takes the location and a number object number-1 .. number-4 (operator arguments are objects).
##
## Search control generated from the structure of the description (World-Conventions L21-001; not stated in the English):
##   each location gets exactly one write, and these commute, so write is proposed only for the first location still without one,
##   in the order of the initial world (empty-first, moved along empty-next).
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute location 25
production optimize-attribute task 25
production optimize-attribute group 25
production optimize-attribute object 25
production optimize-attribute empty 4
production optimize-attribute member 16
production optimize-attribute empty-next 3
production optimize-attribute empty-first 2


## Propose initialize-color-ken-ken when its conditions below hold.
sp {color-ken-ken*propose*initialize-color-ken-ken
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-color-ken-ken ^task-operator false)
}

